    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40db05a8_f2bb9fca",
        "filename": "media/module/extractors/midi/MidiExtractor.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 368,
      "author": {
        "id": 1546599
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-01T14:22:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have tried to match the library in terms of what is required.\n\n\u003e not checking that title field is non-empty (and alphanumeric]\n\nAs per\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/sonivox/arm-wt-22k/lib_src/eas_rtttl.c;l\u003d1049;drc\u003d48dd86efcb221f80bb4558e5f6be400f5e49dcb5\n\n- There is no need for the bytes in the title to be alphanumeric.\n- The first byte can be \u0027:\u0027 and it is still valid.\n\n\u003e not checking that the (optional) parameter list ends with a \":\"\n\nI have stopped at parsing \u0027\u003d\u0027. Each command has a different syntax and adding all that parsing logic would make this lot more complicated.\n\nThis is consistent with how \"XMF_\" files are identified (the library actually parses a lot more to determine an XMF_ file correctly).\n\nPlease let me know whether further parsing is necessary, both here and for XMF_ too.\n\nPlease note: As per what is discussed in the bug, the approach here is to identify a file quickly at the risk of a few files wrongly getting identified as midi files.\n\nThe other approach that I had in mind was to reduce the number of readAt() calls by caching the data. Something like aosp/3284284.\nBut that wasn\u0027t a preferred approach as per the discussion in the bug.",
      "parentUuid": "764b3511_7a2c1eda",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 361,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 368,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "f070f10127a75c1e9fef5230c2b8aff26f13f74b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40bcfa8a_a63491b4",
        "filename": "media/module/extractors/midi/MidiExtractor.cpp",
