      "writtenOn": "2024-10-01T13:39:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "doesn\u0027t seem to be correct.\n[based on how our sonivox library behaves. we have no guarantee that the library\nis correct]\n\nI don\u0027t see anything that says OTA_UNICODE must be the final command.\n\n0x1d seems to be \"title is encoded in unicode\".\nlibrary, if it sees 0x22\u003c\u003c1 (OTA_SOUND), it breaks out and declares that\nthe rest is sound, never reading the unicode bit.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 384,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 384,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "f070f10127a75c1e9fef5230c2b8aff26f13f74b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
